# Seat 0 waits on 1s/4s with 1112344s 555z 789p. After drawing the
# winning 1s, seat 0 closes it instead of declaring tsumo. The structural
# waits remain 1s/4s, and 4s is still available. Replacement 7z is outside the wait.
# Seat 1 discards 4s. Mahjong Soul defaults to allowing ron, while Tenhou's
# temporary furiten survives rinshan and blocks ron. Seat 0 passes its pon offer.
# Seat 0's next live draw clears furiten
# and completes the hand on the last 4s.
# Winning sets: 234s, 44s, 555z, 789p and closed kan 1111s.
# The haku gives one han in both branches; Tenhou also adds menzen tsumo.
# Indicators 1z/2z point to absent 2z/3z. No honba or sticks are paid.
# The 4s can finish 234s or the pair. For ron, the higher-paying pair
# reading adds 2 fu: 20 + 10 + 32 + 8 + 2 = 72 -> 80 fu.
# Base 80 * 2^3 = 640; dealer ron rounds 3840 up to 3900.
# On tsumo, 20 + 2 + 32 + 8 + 2 = 64 -> 70 fu, as does 62 fu
# with the ryanmen assignment. Base 70 * 2^4 = 1120;
# dealer tsumo rounds 2240 up to 2300 each = 6900 total.
# Either dealer win repeats East 1 at honba 1.

